## Elastic checks an investigation agent’s answer against traces and a query

Source: Elastic Observability Labs — https://www.elastic.co/observability-labs/blog/apm-root-cause-analysis-ai-agent-service-map
Published: 2026-11-09
Channel: news

Elastic AI Agent investigates production telemetry through a conversational interface. An Elastic walkthrough tests its findings against application performance monitoring records in an instrumented demonstration shop. A checkout alert appears upstream of an injected payment fault, so the investigation must separate the visible symptom from the failing service.

First, the authors attach the alert to the agent’s conversation. Its answer points to payment failures, but expresses uncertainty about whether a particular customer tier is affected. They then open the service map and drill through a transaction into a failing span, the record of one operation within a trace.

Finally, a direct Elasticsearch Query Language query checks the suspected scope: 80 of 138 gold-tier charges failed, while other tiers did not. This is a controlled demonstration with injected faults, not a production incident or a general accuracy benchmark. The article also warns that the agent’s answers vary between runs.

Why it matters: When using agents for incident diagnosis, retain a path from each proposed cause to trace evidence and a reproducible scope check.

